    <string name="flip_conflicts_title">Conflicting words</string>
    <string name="flip_conflicts_hint">Untouched rows keep their outside links. Edit a row to give the flip a copy.</string>
    <string name="flip_conflicts_ok">Flip</string>
    <string name="flip_conflicts_blank">Every conflicting word needs a name</string>
    <string name="flip_conflicts_help">Each row is a word or a translation that reaches past the selection.
        \nA word row lives in containers outside the selection too, so the flip would change them. A translation row is shared with words outside, so the flip would copy it and the sharing would end.
        \nAn untouched row keeps the relation, so everything it reaches outside joins the flip. The check runs again after every round, untouched rows can bring new ones.
        \nAn edited row gives the flip a copy with the new contents, the outside keeps the original.
        \nA space behind the name is the invisible edit: the copy keeps the trimmed name and only the row detaches.
        \nThe cross button drops the words of the row from the flip, nothing changes outside.
        \nA row left in the list without a name refuses the commit. When the list empties, the flip runs.</string>
